  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Manushi Sinde Coffee Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture, Beneficiaries: 350 small holder farmers, of which 103 are women., , The Project Description:, This is an agriculture project located in rural Tanzania on the slopes of Mt Kilimanjaro. This is the leading mild arabica coffee producing region in Tanzania but yet suffers from abject poverty that could be avoided and eliminated completely. This calls for more technical support to the organization, use the available resources more optimally and improve the governance set up. The project entails extending an organizational assistance grant to enhance the capacity of the project to grow better varieties of coffee, improve coffee quality, ensure timely procurement of agri-inputs, ensure timely payment for farmers coffee upon delivery at the cooperative and ensure improved governance and financial management and control. The expected outcomes include higher incomes for better quality coffee, improved productivity to ensure more quality coffee is produced form the same area under cultivation. The project will also entail embracing other cross-cutting issues including environmental conservation, HIV aids awareness and alcohol abuse.</narrative>
  </description>
